  "verbalization": "Theasaponin E1 is implicated in the regulation of Tyrosine-protein kinase Lyn through a complex network of targets. The evidence suggests that Theasaponin E1 acts as a target for multiple proteins, including Solute carrier organic anion transporter family member 2A1, Dual specificity testis-specific protein kinase 1, and ES1. All these proteins are ultimately targeted by a common compound, [(3S,9S,12R,13R,14R,15R)-13-hydroxy-6-(1-hydroxyethyl)-12,14-dimethyl-2,5,8,11-tetraoxo-9-(propan-2-yl)-15-tridecyl-1-oxa-4,7,10-triazacyclopentadecan-3-yl]methyl acetate, which is known to interact with Tyrosine-protein kinase Lyn. This indicates that Theasaponin E1 may exert its effects through a shared mechanism, possibly by modulating the activity of these downstream targets. The high scores in the evidence suggest a strong and consistent relationship, though the exact molecular pathway remains to be fully elucidated.",
